cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AGHC-S128 Reproducibility Package: Adaptive Graph Hill Cipher with Shift-128 Residual Processing"
message: >-
  If this reproducibility package or the baseline algorithm contributed to
  your work, please cite both the original paper and this software artifact.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Wijonarko"
    given-names: "Dwi"
    email: "dwi-wijonarko@unej.ac.id"
    affiliation: "Universitas Jember"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dwi-wijonarko-unej/aghc-s128-reproducibility"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22928979"
    description: "Zenodo archive (version 1.0.0)"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility implementation of the AGHC-S128 research cipher
  (Adaptive Graph Hill Cipher with Shift-128 Residual Processing).
  Provides the baseline-faithful core algorithm, statistical evaluation
  metrics, experiment pipelines, CLI, regression tests against the original
  Colab notebook implementation, and documentation of known limitations.
  This is a research prototype; statistical evaluations do not constitute a
  cryptographic security proof (see docs/SECURITY_SCOPE.md).
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - research software
  - cipher
  - hill-cipher
  - chaos
  - statistical-evaluation
